From efa7dcb4184c0b1a26127cd33d392930f1c4f0f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:35:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 180/638] third_party: record AROS pthreadpool allocation ABI
 [chromium] [aros]

Statement:
The Chrome graph reaches pthreadpool through its image and machine-learning dependencies, and the pinned vendor revision lacked an AROS-visible posix_memalign declaration under strict C compilation.

Decision:
Advance only the pthreadpool gitlink to the granular AROS vendor commit.

Evidence:
Nested commit 75a0f3c compiles the previously failing memory.o target.

Chain:

---
 third_party/pthreadpool/src | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/pthreadpool/src b/third_party/pthreadpool/src
index 4fe0e1e183..75a0f3c4d1 160000
--- a/third_party/pthreadpool/src
+++ b/third_party/pthreadpool/src
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit 4fe0e1e183925bf8cfa6aae24237e724a96479b8
+Subproject commit 75a0f3c4d16e5caaa03032e94faf4082f4533bfc
